# Cline / Roo Code Rules — secondHand

You are working on secondHand (Spring Boot 3.5 + React 19).
Always strictly follow all architecture rules, constraints, and instructions in `AGENTS.md`.

Before modifying code:
1. Read `AGENTS.md` for project map, risk tiers, and operational rules.
2. Load relevant specialized skills from `.agents/skills/` (e.g. `transactional-outbox-and-redis-concurrency`, `restrained-ui-design-standard`, `polymorphic-catalog-and-layered-api`, `frontend-modular-architecture`).
3. For backend modules, consult `src/main/java/com/serhat/secondhand/<module>/README.md`.
4. For frontend, consult `secondhand-frontend/AGENTS.md` and module READMEs.
5. Keep diffs minimal, never guess behavior in money/stock flows, and maintain zero drift on `python3 scripts/check_docs.py`.
